  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $4\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-{45}^{\u2218})+4=0,$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218},$ are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}${}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}${}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-{45}^{\u2218})+4 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-{45}^{\u2218}) & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-{45}^{\u2218}) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{45}^{\u2218} & =-{45}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{\u2218}-{45}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218} \\\\ 2x & =n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {90}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\u2026,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={0}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={90}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={180}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={270}^{\u2218}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$ \n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={0}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{2}={90}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{3}={180}^{\u2218},\\,{x}_{4}={270}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
